WEBVTT

00:00.504 --> 00:03.935
Let's say that you are
desperate for a dollar.

00:03.935 --> 00:06.763
So you come to me the local loan shark,

00:06.763 --> 00:08.805
and you say hey I need
to borrow a dollar for

00:08.805 --> 00:11.603
a year. I tell you I'm
in a good mood, I willing

00:11.603 --> 00:14.516
to lend you that dollar
that you need for a

00:14.516 --> 00:17.008
year. I will lend it to
you for the low interest

00:17.008 --> 00:25.734
of 100% per year. 100% per year.

00:25.734 --> 00:28.348
How much would you have
to pay me in a year?

00:28.348 --> 00:30.203
You're going to have to pay the original

00:30.203 --> 00:33.941
principal what I lent
you plus 100% of that.

00:33.941 --> 00:37.435
Plus one other dollar.
Which is clearly going

00:37.435 --> 00:44.349
to be equal to $2. You
say oh gee, that's a lot

00:44.349 --> 00:48.468
to have to pay to pay back
twice what I borrowed.

00:48.468 --> 00:50.942
There's a possibility that
I might have the money

00:50.942 --> 00:54.537
in 6 months. What kind
of a deal could you get

00:54.537 --> 00:56.470
me for that Mr. Loanshark?

00:56.470 --> 00:58.742
I say oh gee, if your
willing to pay back in

00:58.742 --> 01:01.074
6 months, then I'll
just charge you half the

01:01.074 --> 01:03.146
interest for half the time.

01:03.146 --> 01:10.284
You borrow one dollar,
so in 6 months, I will

01:10.284 --> 01:18.111
charge you 50% interest.
50% interest over 6 months.

01:18.111 --> 01:22.691
This, of course, was 1
year. How much would you

01:22.691 --> 01:24.868
have to pay? Well, you
would have to pay the

01:24.868 --> 01:26.872
original principal what you borrowed.

01:26.872 --> 01:29.601
The one dollar plus
50% of that one dollar.

01:29.601 --> 01:35.299
Plus 0.50, and that of
course is equal to 1.5.

01:36.037 --> 01:39.923
That is equal to $1.50. I'll
just write it like this.

01:39.923 --> 01:44.087
$1.50. Now you say well
gee that's I guess better.

01:44.087 --> 01:46.524
What happens if I don't
have the money then?

01:46.524 --> 01:49.060
If I still actually need a year.

01:49.060 --> 01:51.667
We actually have a system for that.

01:51.667 --> 01:53.858
What I'll do is just
say that okay, you don't

01:53.858 --> 01:56.004
have the money for me
yet. I'll essentially ...

01:56.004 --> 01:57.756
we could think about it.
I will just lend that

01:57.756 --> 02:00.937
amount that you need for
you for another 6 months.

02:00.937 --> 02:02.751
We'll lend that out.

02:02.751 --> 02:05.798
We'll lend that out for
another 6 months at the

02:05.798 --> 02:10.837
same interest rate at 50%
for the next 6 months.

02:10.837 --> 02:17.324
Then you'll owe me the
principal a $1.50 plus

02:17.324 --> 02:24.314
50% of the principal, plus 75
cents. Plus 75 cents, and that

02:24.314 --> 02:30.517
gets us to $2.25. That equals $2.25.

02:30.517 --> 02:33.295
Another way of thinking
about it is to go from

02:33.295 --> 02:35.514
$1 over the first
period, you just multiply

02:35.514 --> 02:38.715
that times 1.5. If your
going to grow something

02:38.715 --> 02:41.747
by 50%, you just multiply it times 1.5.

02:41.747 --> 02:43.807
If your going to grow it
by another 50%, you can

02:43.807 --> 02:46.127
multiply by 1.5 again.

02:46.127 --> 02:48.400
One way of thinking about
it that 50% interest is

02:48.400 --> 02:51.271
the same thing as multiplying by 1.5.

02:51.271 --> 02:53.397
Multiplying by 1.5.

02:53.397 --> 02:58.448
If you start with 1 and
multiply by 1.5 twice,

02:58.448 --> 03:00.804
this is going to be the same thing.

03:00.804 --> 03:06.399
$2.25 is going to be 1
multiplied by 1.5 twice.

03:06.399 --> 03:12.021
1.5 multiplied twice is the
same thing as 1.5 squared.

03:12.021 --> 03:13.801
You can see the same
thing right over here.

03:13.801 --> 03:17.281
This is the same thing.
100% is the same thing

03:17.281 --> 03:22.997
